From fa0874eb65cdca5246b3fb9cd5150f537ef93225 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:15:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Keep the second critic-blind screen's build, approval,
 reading, checks and report

Adds docs/investigations/stance_2026_10/bias_screen2/ (324 files, about
1.8 MB) with a README: the second critic-blind screen of decision
D-D57, from its build and criteria to its reading, final, its two
independent checks and the report, each a copy of the file at the same
path in the screen's session-scratch folder
(scratchpad2/r10round/bias_screen2/; each run_logs/ is the logs/ beside
it). Eight CPU continuations of stance6_r10LTSB_s42 from its 2,097,152
checkpoint to 3,538,944 (175 updates), 4 control and 4
critic_blind_tail3, paired seeds 2501 to 2531, on the first screen's
sealed code copy:

- criteria.txt (sha256 291ff457..., APPROVED's criteria_sha256),
  APPROVED (184f9ab9..., the run log's pin, written at 12:53:50 UTC, 46
  s before the first start), SCREEN.json and the builder's
  SHA256SUMS.txt; NOTES.txt (the first screen's tools re-pointed at
  2,097,152); REPORT.md, the result as reported at 16:22 UTC with the
  checkers' wording corrections S-2 to S-7;
- tools/: the six pinned tools (run_bs.py gzipped) with their five test
  files and two helpers; check_build/: the independent build check (0
  blocking); criteria_work/: the designer's and the scorer adapter's
  notes and scripts;
- review/: the design and process reviews (0 blocking, 32 findings),
  the fixer's record (31 confirmed, 25 fixed) and the re-review of the
  fixed version (READY TO PIN, 0 blocking, one minor finding handled by
  procedure);
- runs/<name>/, run_logs/ (decided.tsv: all 8 COUNTED; the empty crash
  ledger; the access-time snapshot taken at ALL_DECIDED) and reads/;
- score/: score_bs 2.1, run once at 15:57:01 UTC: STATUS final; line 2,
  "REDUCED: BLINDING THE CRITIC TO THE TAIL_3 ANGLE (observation 6)
  REDUCED THE ON-POLICY TAIL_3 COMMAND OVER THE LAST 8 UPDATES BEFORE
  E, FROM s42's 2,097,152 STATE (exact one-sided permutation test, p
  <= 0.05)": control +0.67001, +0.79227, +0.51081 and +0.41938 against
  blinded +0.14283, +0.12485, +0.13810 and +0.06516; the control median
  rise +0.46382 against the 0.20 gate; p 1/70;
- check/stat/ and check/proc/: the two independent checks (both agree,
  0 blocking; 104 comparisons with score.json, 0 differences).

Every copy is byte-identical to its source, absolute session-scratch
paths included, but for two existing kinds of change. redact: one
workflow run id in criteria_work/DESIGN_NOTES.txt (after the word
"workflow"), and in four of the process check's transcript reads 3
workflow run ids (2 distinct), 1 scheduled-task id and 8 background-job
ids of the session's task runner (4 distinct); criteria.txt (its line 5)
and APPROVED (its line 13) keep the one workflow run id each holds,
since their sha256 are the approved pin and the run log's. gzip:
tools/run_bs.py, as in bias_screen/; gunzip restores it, and then
sha256sum -c --ignore-missing SHA256SUMS.txt gives 24 files OK (26 where
the session's scratch holds the start checkpoint's two files, which it
lists by their absolute paths) and the six tools equal APPROVED's
tool_sha256. Every source's sha256 equals its entry in the SHA256SUMS of
the screen's durable copy (claude/handoff-bias-screen2 at 2d241410, read
in its local clone), but that of
review/process/work/copyroot_sha256.txt, which that copy's name filter
left out. Not copied: each continuation's checkpoints, ledger, training
episodes, policy probe, arm evidence per rollout and other run records;
the reads' JSON and the reader's cache; the validations; the drafts and
the reviews' copies; the synthetic roots and pytest temporaries; the
trainer's temporary files; the process check's raw access-time scan
(1,073,346 bytes, over the 500 KB limit for an added file); 47 empty
files; the runner's lock file and process-table snapshots; and two
listings of the container's files outside the session's folders. The
durable branch holds all of these that are text but the training
episodes, the validations' ledgers, the dry-run roots dryrun_root/ and
copyroot/ and the empty lock file. 2 JSON files without a final newline
and 27 files with lines ending in spaces are kept as their sources have
them; the README names them. The Python scripts parse on Python 3.11,
3.12 and 3.13.

SOURCES.txt gains the note and 324 rows; SHA256SUMS now pins 2002
files (sha256sum -c: all OK); the folder's README gains the entry, the
folder's note under "What changed in the copies", the README among the
files SHA256SUMS does not pin, and four re-check rows; this change's
status row names the folder.

Records only: no library code, configuration, test, notebook, digest or
generated file changes.

